{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The words of this covenant.</b> 'Cursed is the man who makes,' etc. — those stated in the portion כי תבא." "<b>And blesses himself.</b> Language of blessing: when he hears the curse, he blesses <b>in his heart</b> and says, <b>'Peace shall be to me'</b> — like a person who, when he hears the curse, says, 'except for me.'" "<b>[And blesses himself in his heart.</b> He makes himself out to be blessed.]" "<b>For in the stubbornness of my heart I walk.</b> If in the stubbornness of my heart." "<b>To add the watered.</b> To multiply transgressions: those that his soul drinks and is sated by, in which there is no evil inclination, such as wearing shaatnez and similar things. <b>The thirsty</b> — [with the thirsty]: with the transgressions that his soul desires and thirsts for, such as robbery and forbidden relations and similar things. Another interpretation: <b>To add the watered with the thirsty</b> — to add and sate with satiety of transgressions one who is hungry and thirsty for them; that is, when will a day come to transgress in public, so that he can sate himself with what he thirsts for today, for he fears lest he be judged by those who have power in their hands. Another interpretation: to add and join the righteous with the wicked and make like their deeds — the verse likened the righteous to 'watered' on account of 'והיתה נפשם כגן רוה,' and the wicked to 'thirsty' on account of 'והיה כערער בערבה.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:47.143451416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}